From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:06:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GUIWindowVideo: leave video views without waiting on artwork

Leaving a video window called StopThread() on the thumb loader, joining it
on the GUI thread until a slow share answered. Ask it to stop without
joining, as before playback; the next Load() joins it. The window is only
deactivated and ignores the loader's results; shutdown still joins, as the
texture cache is torn down first. CGUIWindowVideoNav stops the loader
itself, so it changes too. Shared GUI code with no Amlogic counterpart.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
index 2584ba7256955a6c858e29eb5820f82f490fed40..fbc76542044899e9027ffd54e92781f9f48470e5 100644
--- a/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/windows/GUIWindowVideoBase.cpp
@@ -131,8 +131,16 @@ bool CGUIWindowVideoBase::OnMessage(CGUIMessage& message)
   switch ( message.GetMessage() )
   {
   case GUI_MSG_WINDOW_DEINIT:
+    // Don't wait for the item being loaded: on a slow share that read can take tens
+    // of seconds. The window stays alive, and the loader is joined before reuse. At
+    // shutdown it has to finish now, before the services it uses are torn down.
     if (m_thumbLoader.IsLoading())
-      m_thumbLoader.StopThread();
+    {
+      if (g_application.IsStopping())
+        m_thumbLoader.StopThread();
+      else
+        m_thumbLoader.StopAsync();
+    }
     m_database.Close();
     break;
 
